            <ArticleTitle>Bupivacaine as pre-emptive analgesia in third molar surgery: Randomised controlled trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>501-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We conducted a prospective, randomised study on the use of pre-emptive analgesia in 45 patients who had bilateral impacted third molars removed. Bupivacaine 0.5% with adrenaline 1:200,000 was injected on one side, the other side acting as control. A visual analogue scale was used to measure the extent of postoperative pain. There was a significant reduction (p = 0.05) in postoperative pain on the injected side at 6, 12, and 72 h and an overall reduction in pain up to 7 days.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
